<p>Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan met Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky in Istanbul on April 4 for talks centered on efforts to end Russia&#x27;s war in Ukraine, along with Black Sea navigation security and energy supply issues. The meeting came a day after Erdogan spoke with Russian President Vladimir Putin, who accused Kyiv of trying to target a gas pipeline that links Russia and Turkiye and supplies some European countries. According to the Turkish presidency, the leaders also discussed bilateral ties and wider regional developments. Zelensky said they reviewed possible joint projects in gas infrastructure and opportunities to jointly develop gas fields. On a parallel diplomatic track, Kyiv said US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner could visit Ukraine in April, and Zelensky said Ukraine was willing to hold the next round of talks with Russia and the United States in Turkiye.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/8dLYjLILjhwZ5WhL6YC0-1Hs9U3V7EqDJGRg8z0dIbyTQLeujllbWJPWuev7OVqCZ2h_rq831d9nWt-RI8M30lFhXvVx8qkqjIvrdOyem-K3' alt='Turkiye’s President Recep Tayyip Erdogan and Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelensky attend a bilateral meeting on security at Dolmabahce Presidential Office in Istanbul on April 4.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Meeting venue: The talks took place at Istanbul&#x27;s Dolmabahce Palace, which previously hosted several rounds of negotiations between Moscow and Kyiv.</li><li>US channel: Kyiv said US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner could visit Ukraine in April as part of a push to restart diplomacy.</li></ul><blockquote>Steps to implement joint projects in developing gas infrastructure, as well as opportunities for joint development of gas fields - Volodymyr Zelensky</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Turkish presidency: Ankara said Erdogan emphasized the importance of safe Black Sea navigation and secure energy supplies during the Istanbul talks. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988644/erdogan-zelensky-discuss-peace-efforts'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian government: Kyiv said it was ready for another round of talks with Russia and the United States and supported Turkiye as a possible host. (<a href='https://newsukraine.rbc.ua/news/t-rkiye-steps-in-to-host-next-round-of-ukraine-1775328416.html'>RBC Ukraine</a>)</li><li>Russian government: Moscow said it wants a permanent settlement and does not see a brief holiday truce as enough without clearer proposals from Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988644/erdogan-zelensky-discuss-peace-efforts'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988644/erdogan-zelensky-discuss-peace-efforts'>Erdogan, Zelensky discuss peace efforts</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-could-visit-ukraine-kyiv-says'>Ukraine expects top US envoys in Kyiv in April to reboot talks</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://newsukraine.rbc.ua/news/t-rkiye-steps-in-to-host-next-round-of-ukraine-1775328416.html'>Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelenskyy says that Ukraine is willing to hold the next round of peace talks with Russia and the United States.</a> - rbc.ua</li></ul>